    "body": "Alright, the PR is almost ready.\r\n\r\nThere is one last thing I want to address.\r\n\r\nCurrently, the remote tracking branch name is added at the end of the local branch name, **after truncation**.\r\n\r\nIt means that if the local branch name is `git_branch_remote_branch_name`, truncated to `git_branch...`, the final branch name would be `git_branch...:remote_name`.\r\n\r\nThe downside is that it _kind of_ conflicts with the truncation purpose, since it is not possible to control the overall length of the string without completely disabling the remote branch feature.\r\n\r\nIf I append the remote branch name *before* truncation, it makes no sense.\r\n\r\nWhat would you recommend ?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
